{"id": "558122ac-bb51-4dd5-8965-f8ca051f8ef4", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "This seems like enough to answer with appropriate caveats. On Bedrock, the Converse API's InferenceConfiguration covers temperature (0-1), topP, and maxTokens, while topK lives in additionalModelRequestFields for certain models. Seed support isn't universal and varies by model, so I should point to checking each model's specific inference parameters—and even with temperature at 0, results aren't guaranteed to be bit-identical due to floating point and backend variability.

I should also mention that using a pinned model ID rather than a "latest" alias or cross-region inference profile matters, since those could route to different hardware, and I could offer to help check invocation logs.

